   squarefree d = 7 mod 8 (2 splits in Q(sqrt(-d))), d <= 20000, with class number 1: [7]
   norm lemma: if p splits in Q(sqrt(-d)) with h = 1 then p = x^2 + xy + ((d+1)/4) y^2 with y != 0, so p >= (d+1)/4:
     d =   7: smallest split prime   2;  (d+1)/4 =   2;  equal: True
     d =  11: smallest split prime   3;  (d+1)/4 =   3;  equal: True
