== 6. Ordinary elliptic curves over F_2, and E_7 = 49a1 over F_(2^k)
   16 smooth Weierstrass tuples over F_2; ordinary (trace odd): 8, all with a1 = 1: True;  traces [(-1, 4), (1, 4)];  Frobenius discriminants a^2 - 8: [-7]
   supersingular (trace even): [(-2, 2), (0, 4), (2, 2)]  -> every ordinary curve over F_2 has Frobenius (+-1 +- sqrt(-7))/2 in Q(sqrt(-7)); x^2 - x + 2 has roots -g, -conj(g)
   #E_7(F_(2^k)), k = 1..8, direct count: {1: 2, 2: 8, 3: 14, 4: 16, 5: 22, 6: 56, 7: 142, 8: 288}   matches 2^k + 1 - t_k (t_k = t_(k-1) - 2 t_(k-2)): True
   k <= 36 with 7 | #E_7(F_(2^k)): [3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36]   = multiples of 3: True
   (Frobenius pi = 1 + g acts on the 7-isogeny kernel E[sqrt(-7)] = Z/7 as multiplication by 4 = 2^(-1), an element of order 3 of <2>)

