== 12. Ramanujan tau mod 7 (and mod 49 on the non-residues)
   tau(1..10) mod 49 agree with the known values: True
   tau(n) = n sigma_9(n) mod 7 for all n <= 6000: True ;  mod 49 for all n = 3,5,6 mod 7: True   (mod 49 fails for 1379 other n <= 6000)
   residues mod 7 of primes p <= 6000 with tau(p) = 0 mod 7: [0, 3, 5, 6] ;  with tau(p) != 0 mod 7: [1, 2, 4] True
   tau(p) = 2p mod 7 for p = 1,2,4 mod 7: True ;  mechanism: tau(p) = p + p^4 = p(1 + p^3) mod 7 and p^3 = (p/7) mod 7 (Euler, exponent 3 = (7-1)/2)

