== 14. Landau-Ramanujan constant of Q(sqrt(-7))
   C_7 = (1/sqrt(pi)) * sqrt( L(1,chi_-7) * 7/6 * prod_{q=3,5,6 mod 7} (1-q^-2)^-1 ) = 0.724719515604  (Euler product truncated at 2*10^6)
   control: Landau-Ramanujan K (sums of two squares) by the same formula = 0.764223647406  (known 0.764223653589...)
   B_7(1e+04) = 2596;  B * sqrt(log x)/x = 0.78785
   B_7(1e+05) = 22737;  B * sqrt(log x)/x = 0.77148
   B_7(1e+06) = 204805;  B * sqrt(log x)/x = 0.76124
   B_7(1e+07) = 1880073;  B * sqrt(log x)/x = 0.75480
   (B_7(x) counts n <= x of the form x^2 + xy + 2y^2; convergence to C_7 is slow, with a 1/log x correction, as for sums of two squares)

